{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 969,
    "dDurationMs": 5531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the most revolutionary things we learned\nin the 20th century was that time is not absolute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6500,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– the rate at which time passes for you\n(or anything else in the universe) is different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9080,
    "dDurationMs": 3070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depending on how fast you're moving and how\nmuch you're accelerating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12150,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In particular: time passes slower the more\nyou're moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15590,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This fact has been confirmed experimentally\ncountless times – fast-moving muons take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19960,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "longer to decay, light emitted from a moving\nsource has a lower frequency , and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24650,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But relativity of time can at first glance\nseem somewhat contradictory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28849,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suppose we're flying past each other; from\nmy perspective it seems like you're moving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32770,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(and so time should go more slowly for you),\nand from your perspective it seems like I'm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36790,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moving (and so time should go more slowly\nfor me)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39650,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems crazy that we can both think time\nis going slower for the other person – someone's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44300,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time must actually be slower, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46790,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, no - take a look at my giraffe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48610,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's 3 meters tall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50310,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And your giraffe is 3 meters tall, according\nto you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53790,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you're rotated relative to me, so you\nonly measure my giraffe to be 2 meters high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58510,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I'm rotated relative to you, so I only\nmeasure your giraffe to be 2 meters high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62860,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we each think the other is measuring distances\nin space as longer, but it's not a contradiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67690,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just that we've rotated height and width\nrelative to each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70820,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And similarly, when you change your speed,\nyou rotate the direction of time – I have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75250,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another video explaining why."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77030,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it looks like this: if every passing second\nI move to the left, then my clock will tick"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81570,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82640,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if every passing second you move to the\nright, then your clock will tike like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87140,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when three seconds have passed on my clock,\nI'll measure only two seconds having passed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91920,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet when three seconds have passed on\nyour clock, you'll measure only two seconds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95280,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "having passed for me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96770,
    "dDurationMs": 5510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we each think the other is measuring distances\nin time as shorter, but it's not a contradiction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102280,
    "dDurationMs": 4301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's just how time behaves when it's rotated –\nit affects not just the passage of time, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106581,
    "dDurationMs": 2359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also our notions of \"the same time\" ."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108940,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, there's still an unanswered question:\nwhat if I stay on earth and you go off into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112810,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space and then come back?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115060,
    "dDurationMs": 4239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Will one of us have actually aged more, or\nwill we both have aged the same amount despite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119299,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "constantly thinking the other was aging less?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121869,
    "dDurationMs": 4031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This conundrum is called the Twins Paradox,\nand I'll explain the solution to it in my"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125900,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "next video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126920,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the meanwhile, can you use rotating\ntime to figure out why the twins paradox isn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131130,
    "dDurationMs": 37420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a paradox?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
